      "dimensionKey": "overall",
      "minScore": 0,
      "maxScore": 30,
      "title": "Developing",
      "description": "Holding a spoken sequence in mind — especially in reverse — is difficult right now, and minimally-different word pairs are easy to mishear.",
      "recommendations": [
        "Practice with shorter sequences first (3-4 digits) before attempting longer ones",
        "For backward spans, try picturing the digits appearing one at a time, then read them off in reverse from that mental image",
        "Listen for the specific sound that differs in word pairs (first sound, middle vowel, last sound) rather than judging the whole word at once"
      ],
      "order": 1
    },
    {
      "dimensionKey": "overall",
      "minScore": 31,
      "maxScore": 50,
      "title": "Average",
      "description": "Shorter spans are manageable, but longer sequences and backward recall specifically show real strain.",
      "recommendations": [
        "Backward span is meant to be substantially harder than forward — a big gap between the two is normal, not a red flag",
        "Practice minimal-pair listening specifically (many free speech-perception exercises use exactly this format)"
      ],
      "order": 2
    },
    {
      "dimensionKey": "overall",
      "minScore": 51,
      "maxScore": 70,
      "title": "Strong",
      "description": "Reliable recall across most sequence lengths, both forward and backward, with solid auditory discrimination.",
      "recommendations": [
        "Push toward longer sequences (7+ digits) to find your actual ceiling",
        "Notice whether forward or backward span is your relative strength — that's informative about your auditory working-memory style"
      ],
      "order": 3
    },
    {
      "dimensionKey": "overall",
      "minScore": 71,
      "maxScore": 85,
      "title": "Very Strong",
      "description": "Strong auditory working memory in both directions, plus fast, accurate discrimination of similar-sounding words.",
      "recommendations": [
        "This is a genuine asset for verbal-heavy, listening-intensive work — meetings, interpretation, live instruction-following",
        "Compare this with your visual/spatial memory results — auditory and visual working memory don't always track together"
      ],
      "order": 4
    },
    {
      "dimensionKey": "overall",
      "minScore": 86,
